From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:46:07 +0200
Subject: glm: A and C on the E4M3 image (patch 0205 stacked on 0206/0208):
 exl3-prompt-once-e4m3 and glm-exl3-fuse-e4m3, tf-cuda-test builds again

TF_GLM_PF_EXPERTS_ONCE's tf_exl3_prompt_gu_once and TF_GLM_PF_DOWN_FUSE's fused down decode only through
exl3_prompt.cuh's mcg2 / decode_a8 / decode_ag / decode_lane, which carry TF_EXL3_MCG_E4M3, so the exl3_experts_e4m3
image already holds them on EXLR8's values; no kernel or engine change. New GPU tests prove it:
  exl3-prompt-once-e4m3 [DIR]  the 12 once cases on the E4M3 image (DIR: an up1 layer.bin whose manifest says
                               mcg_e4m3), each with controls: the K4 image's unfused bytes differ, and so do the
                               K4 image's once kernel's against the E4M3 unfused result
  glm-exl3-fuse-e4m3           the 45 fused-down cases on the E4M3 image, with the same K4-image controls
tf-cuda-test did not compile on 0205 (glm_exl3_layer_tests' Loader had no has(), glm_loader_gate's Modules.load
lacked the e4m3 argument): fixed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQVvNktFCvQrvpNUbqtqBX
